  The prompt's idealized output path is apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Analytics/WeeklyDigestPage.swift,
  but the REAL Xcode project (project.yml) compiles app sources from apps/apple/Sources/** — the
  TeslaSync/Features/** subtree is NOT a build input, and .swiftlint.yml's `included:` does not list it.
  Every already-DONE sibling analytics page (Mileage / Statistics / FleetCompare / LifetimeStats /
  TrueCost / Timeline / YearReview) lives under apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/. Placing the page
  there is what actually compiles, registers, lints, and is gate-covered; the alternative would be a
  non-compiled, non-registered stub (covenant #4). Files therefore live under
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/** + the matching Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/ test dir.

SCOPE NOTE (no scope narrowing, covenant #2)
  The manifest record for this page is "thin" (PARITY_REQUIRED=8 = 3 states + 5 strings; it lists no
  panels / charts / data sources because the page delegates to sub-components + a non-API hook the
  generator could not introspect). The web page is in fact rich. Per ADR-011 ("no stubs as final") and
  the acceptance criterion "reproduce every region from the web source", the FULL web surface was
  implemented natively: WeekSelector, SummaryHeroCards (5 hero metrics + fun-fact), DrivingSection
  (daily-distance bar chart + 4 efficiency mini-stats + top-drive card/empty), ChargingSection
  (daily-energy bar chart + 4 charging mini-stats + energy-vs-last-week chip), BatteryHealthSection
  (2 battery pills + 3 range mini-stats), AlertsSection (severity list + distribution pie / empty), and
  WeekOverWeekSummary (6 trend cards). The 8 binding parity items are a strict subset of this.

