NAVIGATION NOTE (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass)
  The web /weekly-digest route had no pre-existing AppRoute counterpart. A NEW .weeklyDigest case was
  added THROUGH the shared nav infra (a new enum case + its systemImage + group, the two exhaustive
  AppRoute switches). pathSegment maps to "weekly-digest"; AppRouteParser resolves /weekly-digest with
  no alias needed (segment match). MenuCommandCatalog / SpotlightIndexer derive from AppRoute.allCases,
  so route-coverage tests stay green automatically; the segment is unique and the group is .insights.
  TeslaSyncApp composes WeeklyDigestRouteRegistration.registry(.weeklyDigest) into the existing chain;
  no sibling registration, the parser, or any other AppRoute case is displaced.

NAME-COLLISION FINDING + FIX (covenant #1 — reported, not masked)
  The first full xcodebuild surfaced 14 errors, 100% rooted in ONE name collision I introduced: my
  `public enum WeeklyDigestFormat` collided with the PRE-EXISTING `public enum WeeklyDigestFormat` in the
  dashboard widget TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/WeeklyDigestWidget.Adapter.swift (1 "invalid
  redeclaration of 'WeeklyDigestFormat'" root error + 13 cascading "type 'WeeklyDigestFormat' has no
  member 'X'" where the compiler bound my call sites to the widget's formatter). Verified that NONE of my
  other ~30 WeeklyDigest* type names collide with the widget family (WeeklyDigestPageModel vs the widget's
  WeeklyDigestModel, WeeklyDigestDataSource vs WeeklyDigestSource/Telemetry, WeeklyDigestConstants vs
  WeeklyDigestUnitConstants, WeeklyDigestMetrics vs WeeklyDigestMetricRow, etc. — all distinct). FIX:
  renamed my formatter `WeeklyDigestFormat` -> `WeeklyDigestPageFormat` across all my sources + the test +
  renamed the file WeeklyDigestFormat.swift -> WeeklyDigestPageFormat.swift (the widget owns the
  `WeeklyDigest*` adapter namespace there). Re-build: the 14 errors -> 0 (the widget is byte-unchanged).

